From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:02:33 -0300
Subject: drm/amdgpu: expose HDMI 1.4 stereo 3D modes on HDMI connectors and
 emit the vendor infoframe

amdgpu_dm_connector_init_helper() sets connector->stereo_allowed = false,
so every 3D-flagged mode a sink declares in EDID is pruned at probe time
with MODE_NO_STEREO and never reaches userspace. i915, vc4 and nouveau all
allow stereo; amdgpu DC is the outlier among the major drivers, and DC's
HDMI VSIF packet machinery exists but is never populated for these modes.

Allow stereo modes on HDMI connectors and, when a mode carries
DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_*, attach the vendor-specific infoframe that
drm_hdmi_vendor_infoframe_from_display_mode() already computes to the
stream's hfvsif packet so DC emits it. timing_3d_format stays NONE on
purpose: it drives DC's stereo plane-address flipping (kernel-composed
stereo), while compositors, players and games present one already-packed
surface, the same model i915 has used for years. The wire behavior is the
HDMI 1.4a/1.4b stereoscopic framework: the CTA-861 VSIF 3D_Structure codes
(frame packing 0, top-and-bottom 6, side-by-side half 8).

Tested on a Renoir APU (DCN 2.1, Display Core v3.2.369) driving a Sony
KDL-46HX855 (2012) on Linux 7.0: probe goes from 22 modes / 0 stereo to
51 modes / 29 stereo, and modesetting SBS-half 1920x1080@60 makes the set
switch itself into 3D with a visible software-rendered disparity pattern.
Ported to 7.3, where this code moved from amdgpu_dm.c to
amdgpu_dm_connector.c; the change itself is unchanged.

Link: https://github.com/danielcamposramos/sony-bravia-linux (tools, run logs and evidence)
Assisted-by: LLM Kimi K3 (Codex CLI)
Assisted-by: LLM GPT 5.6 Sol (Codex CLI)
Assisted-by: LLM Claude Opus 5 (Claude Code CLI)
(cherry picked from commit c7a8fe0965671ad404f2e8f07888787dfeeb347b)
---
 .../display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c   | 24 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index d386bb1475bb83cf4a16bd5a0ddbb527aa123bfb..587813dc04198e46b1ed8d0f2116151bad26d1d1 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -943,6 +943,28 @@ STATIC_IFN_KUNIT void fill_stream_properties_from_drm_display_mode(
 			drm_warn_once(connector->dev, "Failed to setup vendor infoframe on connector %s: %zd\n",
 				      connector->name, err);
 		timing_out->hdmi_vic = hv_frame.vic;
+
+		/* when the mode carries 3D flags, pack and
+		 * attach the vendor-specific infoframe so a 3D-capable sink
+		 * can switch itself on. Buffer content is composed by
+		 * userspace; timing_3d_format stays NONE on purpose because
+		 * it drives DC's stereo plane-address flip, not the link.
+		 */
+		if (mode_in->flags & DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_MASK) {
+			u8 vsif_raw[32] = { 0 };
+			ssize_t vsif_len;
+
+			vsif_len = hdmi_vendor_infoframe_pack(&hv_frame, vsif_raw,
+							      sizeof(vsif_raw));
+			if (vsif_len >= (ssize_t)(4 + hv_frame.length)) {
+				stream->hfvsif_infopacket.hb0 = vsif_raw[0];
+				stream->hfvsif_infopacket.hb1 = vsif_raw[1];
+				stream->hfvsif_infopacket.hb2 = vsif_raw[2];
+				memcpy(&stream->hfvsif_infopacket.sb[0],
+				       &vsif_raw[3], 1 + hv_frame.length);
+				stream->hfvsif_infopacket.valid = true;
+			}
+		}
 	}
 
 	if (aconnector && amdgpu_dm_is_freesync_video_mode(mode_in, aconnector)) {
@@ -3211,7 +3233,7 @@ void amdgpu_dm_connector_init_helper(struct amdgpu_display_manager *dm,
 	aconnector->dc_link = link;
 	aconnector->base.interlace_allowed = false;
 	aconnector->base.doublescan_allowed = false;
-	aconnector->base.stereo_allowed = false;
+	aconnector->base.stereo_allowed = true;
 	aconnector->base.dpms = DRM_MODE_DPMS_OFF;
 	aconnector->hpd.hpd = AMDGPU_HPD_NONE; /* not used */
 	aconnector->audio_inst = -1;
